 - Fridges must read at or below 5 °C and freezers at or below -15 °C. Each
   of them needs at least one reading per day.
 - Allergens are the 14 EU allergens, stored lowercase and sorted.
+
+## Sites (schema 3)
+
+- `sites` contains records with string `id` and `name`. Each location has a
+  `site` referencing one of these ids; location ids remain globally unique.
+- Schema 2 files migrate by adding site `main` ("Main kitchen") and assigning
+  every existing location to it. Schema 1 files migrate through schema 2.
+  Existing records and stock are preserved.
+- Batches and stock-takes inherit their site from their location. Items,
+  suppliers, recipes and dishes are shared across sites.
+- Stock operations use the store context's site, defaulting to `main`.
+  Request contexts share the complete data and id sequences, so saving one
+  site's changes preserves every site's data.
